Description
Comprehensive documentation for the beast-land-registry repository, detailing its mission to replace municipal property monopolies with cryptographic deeds, system architecture, smart contract workflows, and Google Cloud Run deployment instructions.

Core Code
Markdown
# BEAST Land Registry (`beast-land-registry`)

`beast-land-registry` is a decentralized property and land title management division under the New World Order Private Government framework. It provides a sovereign, tamper-proof alternative to municipal land registries, replacing bureaucratic fees and eminent domain seizure risks with cryptographic land deeds and DAO-managed parcel titles.

---

## 🏗 Repository Architecture

```text
beast-land-registry/
├── contracts/               # Solidity smart contracts for parcel management
│   └── LandRegistry.sol     # On-chain registry for land deeds and ownership transfers
├── backend/                 # Node.js Express API & PostgreSQL database integration
│   ├── src/                 # API routes, database connectors, and parcel handlers
│   ├── db/                  # SQL schema definitions
│   └── Dockerfile           # Cloud Run container configuration
├── frontend/                # Next.js App Router portal for landowners and title checks
├── .github/workflows/       # CI/CD deployment pipeline to Google Cloud Run
└── README.md                # System documentation
🚀 Getting Started
1. Prerequisites
Node.js (>= 20.0.0)

PostgreSQL / Google Cloud SQL instance

MetaMask or compatible Web3 wallet

2. Run Backend Service
Bash
cd backend
npm install
npm run dev
3. Run Frontend Portal
Bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
🏡 Core Principles
Sovereign Ownership: Protects participants from arbitrary municipal property seizures, bureaucratic liens, and inflated recording fees.

Cryptographic Deeds: Immutable parcel titles secured by blockchain transparency and community DAO governance.

Frictionless Transfers: Peer-to-peer property transfers executed instantly via secure smart contracts.
